-- D1C2A runtime #569: exact Student Status P2 guard on
-- approval_applications is SECURITY DEFINER but was created by the narrow
-- schoolos_evidence_writer role. Its integrity checks must read Foundation
-- approval_requests/operation_contracts/command_receipts and D1 immutable
-- status history/student projection; evidence_writer intentionally lacks
-- broad SELECT/RLS on these base tables. Granting it those privileges would
-- break the evidence-writer separation.
--
-- The established Student Identity/Special and Status P1 application guards
-- run as the table's schoolos_schema_owner with the exact existing row-level
-- maintenance policies. Align this one application's INTERNAL trigger owner.
-- Keep the original full guard body, query conditions, and same trigger link.
-- No application/client/user role table or function grants, no disabled RLS,
-- no new function, no changed object/column shape and no executable migration.
--
-- Migration 10 is an INACTIVE .sql.draft concatenation. The local harness
-- executes SQL as postgres (the existing owner-role member), so the owner
-- transfer is performed after a RESET ROLE, without granting role membership.
ALTER FUNCTION app_private.d1_guard_student_status_correct_application()
  OWNER TO schoolos_schema_owner;
